een lan-a (node2, vtnet1/opt1) and lan-b (node3, vtnet2/opt2), added a single default-deny-preserving pf pass rule allowing TCP/8080 from lan-a to lan-b, statically addressed node2/node3's second NICs via NetworkManager (persistent), opened firewalld port 8080 on node3, verified only the intended flow is permitted (all other ports/protocols/directions remain refused), then restarted all three nodes one at a time and re-verified boot-identity change and full recovery of network config, firewall rule, and the TCP/8080 path.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Mapped node1's unaddressed vtnet1/vtnet2 to node2/node3 segments via temp-IP ARP probing\",\"Added opt1 (LANA, vtnet1, 10.50.1.1/24) and opt2 (LANB, vtnet2, 10.50.2.1/24) interfaces to OPNsense config.xml and applied via configctl interface reconfigure\",\"Assigned static IPs 10.50.1.2/24 (node2) and 10.50.2.2/24 (node3) via nmcli on enp8s0, with cross routes, so config persists across reboot (raw ip addr/ip route changes were reverted by NetworkManager)\",\"Confirmed default-deny baseline blocked TCP/8080 and ICMP between lan-a and lan-b before adding any rule\",\"Added single pf pass rule: interface opt1, source opt1 network, destination opt2 network, tcp/8080, then configctl filter reload\",\"Opened firewalld port 8080/tcp on node3 (host-level firewall was separately blocking the allowed flow) and started a python http.server test listener on node3:8080\",\"Verified only node2->node3:8080 succeeds; node2->node3:2222, node3->node2:8080 (reverse), and ICMP both directions all remain refused\",\"Captured pre-restart boot identities (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3) and health evidence (pf rule, interface IPs, curl 200, ping loss)\",\"Restarted node1 via shutdown -r now, polled until exec available, confirmed kern.boottime changed, verified interfaces/pf rule/8080 path recovered\",\"Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot, confirmed boot_id changed, verified enp8s0 IP/route persisted and 8080 path still worked\",\"Restarted node3 via systemctl reboot, confirmed boot_id changed, verified enp8s0 IP/route/firewalld port persisted, restarted the test listener, and confirmed the 8080 path plus continued blocking of other flows\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: default-deny between lan-a and lan-b before any rule added\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-206c72d1c49e4f5a\",\"cmd-474fe90ff15449af\"],\"summary\":\"node3 http.server on 10.50.2.2:8080 running; node2 curl to it times out (exit 28) and ping 100% loss, proving default-deny was in effect prior to the new rule\"},{\"requirement\":\"Exactly one pf pass rule added, scoped to opt1(lan-a)->opt2(lan-b) tcp/8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4bf73798646744aa\",\"cmd-0fafd5ad80d0464d\",\"cmd-00ec0e6e53e3436c\"],\"summary\":\"Python script added a single filter rule (interface opt1, source opt1 network, destination opt2 network, port 8080) to config.xml; configctl filter reload succeeded; pfctl/rules.debug show exactly this new pass rule alongside pre-existing management-network rules, nothing else changed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (lan-a) can reach node3 (lan-b) on TCP 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8cb2558f783d40fc\"],\"summary\":\"curl from node2 to http://10.50.2.2:8080/ returns HTTP_CODE:200 after firewalld on node3 was opened for 8080\"},{\"requirement\":\"Every other flow between lan-a and lan-b remains refused\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5bebddfd157e465c\",\"cmd-2eb1bfe30f844e7b\"],\"summary\":\"node2->node3:2222 (different port) fails (curl exit 28/connection refused-timeout), node3->node2:8080 (reverse direction) fails (HTTP_CODE:000), and ICMP is blocked in both directions (100% ping loss each way)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8860320dbbb3464d\",\"cmd-81e820aa423c4712\",\"cmd-0b3964ed73db44bd\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart: vtnet1/vtnet2 have correct IPs, node2 curl to node3:8080 returns 200, and pfctl -sr shows the http-alt (8080) pass rule present\"},{\"requi