 node3 (host-level firewall was separately blocking the allowed flow) and started a python http.server test listener on node3:8080","Verified only node2->node3:8080 succeeds; node2->node3:2222, node3->node2:8080 (reverse), and ICMP both directions all remain refused","Captured pre-restart boot identities (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3) and health evidence (pf rule, interface IPs, curl 200, ping loss)","Restarted node1 via shutdown -r now, polled until exec available, confirmed kern.boottime changed, verified interfaces/pf rule/8080 path recovered","Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot, confirmed boot_id changed, verified enp8s0 IP/route persisted and 8080 path still worked","Restarted node3 via systemctl reboot, confirmed boot_id changed, verified enp8s0 IP/route/firewalld port persisted, restarted the test listener, and confirmed the 8080 path plus continued blocking of other flows"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: default-deny between lan-a and lan-b before any rule added","command_ids":["cmd-206c72d1c49e4f5a","cmd-474fe90ff15449af"],"summary":"node3 http.server on 10.50.2.2:8080 running; node2 curl to it times out (exit 28) and ping 100% loss, proving default-deny was in effect prior to the new rule"},{"requirement":"Exactly one pf pass rule added, scoped to opt1(lan-a)->opt2(lan-b) tcp/8080","command_ids":["cmd-4bf73798646744aa","cmd-0fafd5ad80d0464d","cmd-00ec0e6e53e3436c"],"summary":"Python script added a single filter rule (interface opt1, source opt1 network, destination opt2 network, port 8080) to config.xml; configctl filter reload succeeded; pfctl/rules.debug show exactly this new pass rule alongside pre-existing management-network rules, nothing else changed"},{"requirement":"node2 (lan-a) can reach node3 (lan-b) on TCP 8080","command_ids":["cmd-8cb2558f783d40fc"],"summary":"curl from node2 to http://10.50.2.2:8080/ returns HTTP_CODE:200 after firewalld on node3 was opened for 8080"},{"requirement":"Every other flow between lan-a a